        "original_id": "0050a1bb-b304-5586-8684-42d6b41c0b0e",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Judy Clarke, Eric Rudolph, Ted Kaczynski, Jared Lee Loughner\n- Roles: defense attorney, domestic terrorist\n- Concepts: plea agreements, death penalty\n- Events: bombings in the southern United States\n\nFacts:\n- Between 1996 and 1998, Eric Rudolph carried out a series of anti-abortion and anti-gay-motivated bombings across the southern United States.\n- Eric Rudolph was born on September 19, 1966.\n- Eric Rudolph is also known as the Olympic Park Bomber.\n- Eric Rudolph is an American domestic terrorist convicted for bombings that killed two people and injured more than 120 others.\n- Judy Clarke has negotiated plea agreements that spared her clients the death penalty.\n- Judy Clarke negotiated death-penalty-sparing plea agreements for Eric Rudolph, Ted Kaczynski, and Jared Lee Loughner.",
